        {
          "title": "Failure Containment Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Failures Spread",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Resilience pattern== = rule limiting how far one bad dependency hurts its callers",
                "**Slow is worse than down**: callers hold threads, sockets, memory while waiting"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Cascading failure",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Service slows",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Caller pools back up",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Timeouts + retries",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Load multiplies upstream",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "System collapses",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Layers, Outer to Inner",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rate limit",
                    "sub": "shed load",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Timeout",
                    "sub": "bound wait",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Retry",
                    "sub": "transient only",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Breaker",
                    "sub": "stop sick calls",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bulkhead",
                    "sub": "isolate",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fallback",
                    "sub": "degrade",
                    "ink": "pink"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Retry or Not",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fault",
                "Examples",
                "Retry?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Transient",
                  "timeout, 503, connection reset, 429",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Permanent",
                  "400, 401, 403, 404",
                  "{red:never}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Little's Law",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==In flight = arrival rate x latency==",
                "100 req/s: 50 ms is 5 in flight, 5 s is 500",
                "**100x** more threads needed, so the pool is exhausted"
              ],
              "style": "number",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**Why is slow worse than down?** Callers wait holding resources. **Which faults to retry?** Transient only, never 4xx."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Timeouts and Retries with Backoff and Jitter",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Timeouts and Retries with Backoff and Jitter",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Timeouts and Deadlines",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every network call needs an ==explicit timeout==",
                "{blue:Connect timeout}: short, ~1 s",
                "{blue:Read timeout}: dependency p99 x 1.5",
                "Default of infinite or 30-60 s = classic outage cause",
                "Pass one ==deadline== down the chain: gRPC deadline, `X-Request-Deadline`",
                "Downstream calls never outlive a caller who gave up"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Backoff and Jitter",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Strategy",
                "Wait",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Backoff",
                  "`min(cap, base x 2^n)`",
                  "100, 200, 400, 800 ms; cap 10 s"
                ],
                [
                  "Full jitter",
                  "`random(0, min(cap, base x 2^n))`",
                  "==Best== load spread (AWS)"
                ],
                [
                  "Equal jitter",
                  "half fixed + half random",
                  "Keeps a minimum wait"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "delay = min(10, 0.1 * 2 ** attempt)",
                "time.sleep(random.uniform(0, delay))"
              ],
              "note": "full jitter"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Backoff gives the dependency room to recover",
                "Jitter breaks **synchronized** retries"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Retry Rules",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cap attempts: usually ==3==",
                "Idempotent operations only, or idempotency keys for POST/payments",
                "Honor `Retry-After`",
                "Retry budget: retries <= ==10%== of requests"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Retry at ONE layer",
              "text": "3 layers x 3 attempts = ==27 calls==. This is retry amplification."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Circuit Breakers and Bulkheads",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
