                  {
                    "from": "h",
                    "to": "o",
                    "label": "any fails"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Failure-rate== and ==slow-call== thresholds",
                "==Minimum calls== before judging the window",
                "Sliding window: count or time based",
                "Open wait; permitted trial calls",
                "One breaker ==per dependency==, not global"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bulkhead",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Own ==bounded pool== per dependency: thread pool or semaphore",
                "e.g. 10 concurrent calls to payments API",
                "Slow dependency exhausts only its own ==compartment== (ship hull)",
                "Pool full: ==reject immediately==, never queue unboundedly"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Breaker vs Bulkhead",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Breaker",
                "Bulkhead"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Trigger",
                  "observed failure",
                  "concurrency cap, up front"
                ],
                [
                  "Limits",
                  "calls, over time",
                  "concurrent damage"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**Breaker states?** Closed, Open, Half-Open. **Why both?** Breaker stops calls after failure; bulkhead caps damage before it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rate Limiting and Load Shedding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rate Limiting and Load Shedding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Limit Per Client",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Caps ==requests per client per window==",
                "Over limit: `429 Too Many Requests` + `Retry-After`",
                "Rate limit protects the {green:server}; breaker protects the {blue:client}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Algorithms",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Algorithm",
                "How",
                "Trait"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Token bucket==",
                  "B tokens, refill R/s, 1 per request",
                  "Burst up to B, avg R; Stripe, AWS"
                ],
                [
                  "Leaky bucket",
                  "Queue drained at fixed rate",
                  "Smooth constant output"
                ],
                [
                  "Fixed window",
                  "Counter per window",
                  "Simplest; 2x burst at boundary"
                ],
                [
                  "Sliding window",
                  "Log or counter",
                  "Fixes burst; more memory"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Distributed Keys",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shared state: Redis `INCR` + `EXPIRE`, or atomic Lua script",
                "Key by user, API key or IP: choose deliberately",
                "Per tenant keys stop ==noisy neighbours=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Load Shedding",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Overloaded: reject ==low-priority work early== with fast `503`",
                "Bounded queue + fast rejection keep accepted latency healthy",
                "Client-side adaptive throttling is the mirror image"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Token vs leaky bucket?** Token allows bursts; leaky smooths output.",
                "**Why shed with 503?** Queueing inflates latency for everyone.",
                "**Fixed window flaw?** 2x burst at boundaries."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fallbacks and Containing Cascading Failures",
      "role": "outline",
